# Imperium architecture rules

These are non-negotiable. Every change must respect them.

## Supabase clients

Three clients exist and they are NOT interchangeable:

- `lib/supabase/client.ts` — browser, anon key, RLS enforced. Use only
  inside Client Components, and only for reads.
- `lib/supabase/server.ts` — Server Components / Server Actions / Route
  Handlers. Bound to the user's session cookie. RLS enforced as that user.
- `lib/supabase/admin.ts` — service role. Bypasses RLS. Marked
  `import "server-only"`. Allowed callers ONLY:
    - Edge Functions in `supabase/functions/*`.
    - Server Actions in `app/admin/*` (after a re-checked admin gate).

Never import `lib/supabase/admin.ts` from a Client Component or from any
shared module that Client Components transitively import. The
`server-only` directive will blow up the build if you do.

## Data mutations

- Mutations go through Server Actions, never direct browser writes.
- Money flows ONLY through `transfer_coins(...)` (Postgres RPC) which
  atomically updates the balance and writes a `ledger_entries` row.
- AP-spending actions check AP and apply the effect in a single SQL
  statement (or a SECURITY DEFINER function). Never read AP, then write
  back from JS — that's a TOCTOU bug.
- Inventory mutations always UPSERT against the
  `(character_id, item_type_id)` unique constraint:

  ```sql
  INSERT INTO inventory (character_id, item_type_id, quantity)
  VALUES ($1, $2, $3)
  ON CONFLICT (character_id, item_type_id)
  DO UPDATE SET quantity = inventory.quantity + EXCLUDED.quantity;
  ```

## Append-only tables

`game_events` is append-only. Triggers in the schema enforce this — any
UPDATE or DELETE raises an exception. To "fix" a bad event, append a
corrective row. Don't try to disable the trigger.

## RLS

RLS is enabled on every public table. Tables without explicit policies
are effectively closed to the anon and authenticated roles. World data
(nodes, cities, counties, etc.) has explicit "FOR SELECT USING (true)"
policies. Don't add tables without thinking through the policy.

## Realtime

Use Realtime ONLY for:
- Clan chat
- Notifications

The map polls — never subscribe to `nodes` or `characters` over Realtime.

## Polymorphic owner columns

Where a column owner can be one of multiple types:

- If all owner types share a column type (e.g. characters and clans both
  use `uuid`), use a single column + `owner_type` discriminator.
- If owner types have different column types (e.g. countries `int` vs
  clans `uuid`), use SEPARATE FK columns guarded by a CHECK that enforces
  exactly one is non-null. See `counties.owner_country_id` /
  `owner_clan_id`.

Don't store FK values as text or untyped int. The schema reflects this.

## Naming and aesthetic

- All colors live in `app/globals.css` as CSS variables, stored as
  space-separated RGB triples and aliased in `tailwind.config.ts` via
  the `rgb(var(--color-X) / <alpha-value>)` pattern. From Tailwind use
  the aliases (`text-gold`, `border-gold/20`). From raw CSS or inline
  SVG attributes use `rgb(var(--color-gold))` — never hardcode hex.
- Display fonts: Cinzel. Body: Lora. Serif: Cormorant Garamond. Don't
  add sans-serif to the design.
- Voice: Byzantine, restrained, occasionally archaic. Not "epic fantasy".

## Sample components for reference

- `components/ui/APBar.tsx` — AP bar pattern
- `components/ui/CoinDisplay.tsx` — coin/gem pair
- `components/character/StatsDisplay.tsx` — stat tile grid

## When you must make a schema change

1. Add a new file `supabase/migrations/00N_<description>.sql`.
2. Update `lib/types/database.types.ts` (run `npm run db:types` if the
   project is linked, otherwise hand-edit).
3. Update `lib/types/game.types.ts` if any composed shape changed.
4. Add or update RLS policies for the new tables.
